id=a52sxq_seccomp
name=Galaxy A52s 5G Samsung Codec2 seccomp: allow mremap(MREMAP_MAYMOVE)
author=kusti420
description=The Samsung software Codec2 HAL (samsung.software.media.c2@1.0-service, arm64) runs under the A14 vendor policy, which only allows `mremap: arg3 == 3` (MREMAP_MAYMOVE|MREMAP_FIXED, the linker CFI shadow). Android 17 bionic's __cxa_atexit (AtexitArray::expand_capacity) grows its handler array with mremap(MREMAP_MAYMOVE) once more than a page of atexit handlers is registered, so the HAL died in a SIGSYS loop at start ("libminijail: blocked syscall: mremap") -> no video decode (setup wizard intro hangs/ANRs). Use the AOSP mediacodec / QTI codec2 rule `mremap: arg3 == 3 || arg3 == MREMAP_MAYMOVE` (same as the upstream Exynos 2100 codec2 rule): the QTI policy already has it, every other vendor policy already allows mremap unconditionally on stock.
